---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Contractor Website Design, Sioux Falls | Couch & Craft"
description: "Websites for Sioux Falls contractors. Show your best projects before the estimate and make it easy for people to call you."
crumb: "Websites for Contractors"
---
{%- set topTeer = site.work | findBySlug("top-teer-construction") -%}
<section class="page-hero band--navy" aria-labelledby="page-heading">
  <div class="container page-hero__inner flow">
    <p class="eyebrow">For contractors and trades</p>
    <h1 id="page-heading">Websites for contractors around {{ site.business.city }}.</h1>
    <p class="page-hero__sub">Your crew does good work. Your site should show it before the estimate.</p>
    <p class="hero__actions">
      <a class="button button--gold" href="/start/" data-track="cta_click" data-label="contractors-hero">Start a project</a>
      <a class="button button--secondary" href="/teardown/">Get a free teardown</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" aria-labelledby="needs-heading">
  <div class="container flow" style="--flow-space: var(--space-l)">
    <h2 id="needs-heading">What a contractor site has to do</h2>
    <ol class="needs">
      <li class="needs__item">
        <h3>Show the work</h3>
        <p>Most people hiring a contractor have never met you. A gallery of finished jobs, with the town and the kind of job, does more than any paragraph about quality. Phone photos are fine if they're sharp and well lit.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="needs__item">
        <h3>Say where you'll drive</h3>
        <p>If you'll take a deck in Harrisburg but not a bathroom in Canton, say so. A clear service area cuts calls you'd turn down anyway and helps Google show you to the right people.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="needs__item">
        <h3>Make the quote easy to ask for</h3>
        <p>A phone number that dials when tapped, and a form short enough to fill out from a driveway. Name, phone, town and what the job is. You can ask the rest on the call.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="needs__item">
        <h3>Use real reviews, when you have them</h3>
        <p>A few real reviews with first names beat a wall of five stars with no names. If you don't have any yet, leave the section off and start asking after every job.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--white" aria-labelledby="anatomy-heading">
  <div class="container flow" style="--flow-space: var(--space-l)">
    <div class="flow">
      <h2 id="anatomy-heading">Anatomy of a contractor homepage</h2>
      <p>{% if topTeer.publish %}How I laid out the {{ topTeer.client }} site, and why.{% else %}Here's the layout I start from. Every business changes it, but these six pieces almost always stay.{% endif %}</p>
    </div>
    {% include "partials/wireframe-contractor.njk" %}
  </div>
</section>

<div class="band">
  <div class="container">
    {%- set faqs = [
      { q: "I get most of my work from referrals. Do I need a website?", a: "<p>Referrals still look you up. Someone hears your name from a neighbor, searches it, and decides in a few seconds whether to call. The site is there for that moment.</p>" },
      { q: "Can you use photos from my phone?", a: "<p>Usually, yes. Sharp phone photos of real jobs beat stock photos. If you don't have many, start taking a few at the end of every job.</p>" },
      { q: "What does it cost?", a: ("<p>Websites start at " + (site.pricing.foundationFrom | open) + ". <a href=\"/pricing/\">See the full pricing</a>.</p>") if ready.pricing else null }
    ] -%}
    {% set faqId = "contractors-faq" %}
    {% include "partials/faq.njk" %}
  </div>
</div>

<section class="band band--white related" aria-label="Keep reading">
  <div class="container related__inner">
    <a class="related__link" href="/web-design/">How I build websites</a>
    <a class="related__link" href="/lead-response/">Answer the calls you miss on a job</a>
    <a class="related__link" href="/work/">See the sites I've built</a>
  </div>
</section>
